<title>USA: U.S. budget may add 15 cents to tobacco tax - source.</title>
<headline>U.S. budget may add 15 cents to tobacco tax - source.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. cigarette taxes will increase by up to 15 cents a pack over the next five years under a budget agreement that Congress and the Clinton administration hope to reach Monday night, a Republican source said.</p>
<p>The federal tax, now 24 cents per pack of 20 cigarettes, would rise 10 cents in the year 2000 and an additional five cents in 2002 under the plan, the aide said.</p>
<p>Bipartisan Senate backers of the tobacco tax hope at least $8 billion of the tax revenue will to go to expand child health-care programs.</p>
</text>
